## Lore

The serpentoids came from the most ruthless corner of Project Achilles, where a
few researchers turned from mammals to reptiles. Convinced that the dread snakes
inspire in other animals had a psychic root, they spliced human DNA with that of
venomous snakes, and the cobra came to dominate the final strain.

Most serpentoids look like a man with a snake''s body fused along his back: a
cobra''s hooded head on a long neck, a spine that bulges outward, and a long
tail. They are lean and wiry but strong, and on a Rifts Earth charged with
psychic energy their empathic gifts grew into a force field able to turn aside
all but heavy military weapons.

The reptilian mind-set left many of them cold and detached. Most learn a code
of honour or the laws of the Republic and respect their fellow citizens, human
or not, but against the nation''s enemies an unsupervised serpentoid may kill or
torture without remorse. Other mutants work beside them, though their eeriness
keeps many away, rodents above all, so most have few friends outside their own
kind.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'serpentoid');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'serpentoid';

